<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Condo Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1820 CE – 1871 CE (approx.) · capital Bopolu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A confederation of Mande, Gola and Vai peoples in north-western Liberia, built by the warrior-trader Sao Boso around the town of Bopolu.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the early 19th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-boso">Sao Boso</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Mandingo</a> warrior and trader known to Europeans as King Boatswain, built a coalition around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bopolu">Bopolu</a> in the hinterland of what is now north-western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/liberia">Liberia</a>. Linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gola-people">Gola</a>, Vai, Dei and other communities, the Condo Confederation aimed to keep the trade routes between the interior and the coast open and safe.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bopolu">Bopolu</a> was a market town where caravans exchanged slaves, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, cloth and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> for salt and European goods from the coast at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-mount">Cape Mount</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monrovia">Monrovia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-boso">Sao Boso</a> and his Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Mandingo</a> allies dominated the confederation, though its members kept their own chiefs. Its relations with the settlers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-liberia">Colony of Liberia</a> mixed trade with occasional conflict.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-boso">Sao Boso's</a> death in 1836 the confederation was weakened by succession quarrels among its leaders and wars between member peoples. By the 1870s its lands came under the claims of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/liberia">Liberia</a>, which absorbed them into the republic's interior.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1820 CE – 1871 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.92%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1820 CE – 1871 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bopolu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sao Boso</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mandinka, Gola, Vai</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/liberia">Liberia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kondo Confederation, Bopolu confederation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1846&amp;focus=condo-confederation" aria-label="Condo Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4390 1913 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Condo Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4710 2169h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4710 2169h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bopolu. <a href="/atlas?year=1846&amp;focus=condo-confederation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

